180
00:14:42,827 --> 00:14:46,036
Your assignment has four questions. One:

181
00:14:46,056 --> 00:14:52,008
a 12-head machine with 1000 newtons of drive. Find the speed limits for 3,

182
00:14:52,028 --> 00:14:54,268
5 and 7 millimetre stitches,

183
00:14:54,288 --> 00:15:00,887
and the minimum drive force that lets the 7 millimetre satin run at 800 r/min too.

184
00:15:01,287 --> 00:15:06,214
Two is about design files, which this video skipped;

185
00:15:06,234 --> 00:15:09,639
it's in the slides and the textbook.

186
00:15:09,659 --> 00:15:14,776
A DST record allows at most 12.1 millimetres per axis.

187
00:15:14,796 --> 00:15:19,533
How many records for a 45 millimetre jump along X,

188
00:15:19,553 --> 00:15:23,053
and for 40 millimetres at 45 degrees?

189
00:15:23,073 --> 00:15:27,334
And how does the machine decide when to trim?

190
00:15:27,734 --> 00:15:31,181
Three: a 12-head machine sews 15 000 stitches.

191
00:15:31,201 --> 00:15:34,195
Estimate efficiency and pieces per hour,

192
00:15:34,215 --> 00:15:39,621
then compare cutting handling to 20 seconds with halving the break rate.

193
00:15:39,641 --> 00:15:43,540
Which is more worth the money? Four is a discussion:

194
00:15:43,560 --> 00:15:48,438
what does cutting the detection delay from 6 stitches to 2 bring,

195
00:15:48,458 --> 00:15:51,754
and how could a detector find breaks faster?

196
00:15:52,154 --> 00:15:57,591
Submit the report and the lab screenshots on the WenQuest platform.

197
00:15:59,111 --> 00:16:07,084
There's also a nine-question quiz. For example, with a 204-degree window,

198
00:16:07,104 --> 00:16:13,326
the shaft at 900 r/min and a 4 millimetre cycloidal move,

199
00:16:13,346 --> 00:16:16,611
what is the peak acceleration?

200
00:16:17,011 --> 00:16:23,600
Or, if the back-up count is smaller than the detection delay, what happens?

201
00:16:23,620 --> 00:16:28,271
Another asks whether a DST file stores colour values.

202
00:16:28,671 --> 00:16:35,171
You get three attempts, and the explanations appear as soon as you submit.

203
00:16:36,691 --> 00:16:38,031
Three things to remember.

204
00:16:38,431 --> 00:16:43,265
One: a multi-head machine shares its shafts and frame,

205
00:16:43,285 --> 00:16:49,197
and each head stops sewing on its own through the needle-bar jump,

206
00:16:49,217 --> 00:16:53,332
trimmer and break detection on its head board.

207
00:16:53,732 --> 00:16:59,571
Two: the frame must finish each move in about a 204-degree window,

208
00:16:59,591 --> 00:17:03,832
available acceleration falls as heads are added,

209
00:17:03,852 --> 00:17:10,401
and the speed limit goes with the root of acceleration over stitch length.

210
00:17:10,801 --> 00:17:16,313
Three: after a break, back up at least the detection delay;

211
00:17:16,333 --> 00:17:22,781
any one break stops every head, so more heads means lower efficiency.

